That suggested a way to give selected project images some of the same energy. In the [cut-paper collage study](/design-lab/collage/), one complete view of the Mangrove Figma library stays visible, with cropped details and a black angular shape around it. The gaps separate the fragments; the main screenshot still makes sense on its own.

I made this an optional figure treatment for posts, used here and in the Johnny Castaway article. The main image and caption stay intact. Small pointer movements shift the decorative layers at different depths; touch devices and reduced-motion settings get a static composition. It is an occasional illustration treatment, while ordinary photographs and thumbnails retain their complete images.

